WEBVTT

00:00.820 --> 00:04.420
Two functions, f and
g, are described below.

00:04.420 --> 00:08.260
Which of these statements
about f and g is true?

00:08.260 --> 00:10.720
So they defined
function f as kind

00:10.720 --> 00:13.560
of a traditional linear
equation right over here.

00:13.560 --> 00:16.070
And this right over here is g.

00:16.070 --> 00:19.150
So this right over
here is g of x.

00:19.150 --> 00:21.530
And that also looks
like a linear function.

00:21.530 --> 00:24.080
We see it's a kind of a
downward sloping line.

00:24.080 --> 00:27.390
So let's look at our choices
and see which of these are true.

00:27.390 --> 00:32.299
f and g are both increasing, and
f is increasing faster than g.

00:32.299 --> 00:34.960
Well, when I look at g--
Well, first of all, g

00:34.960 --> 00:36.390
is definitely decreasing.

00:36.390 --> 00:37.970
So we already know
that that's false.

00:37.970 --> 00:39.660
And f is also decreasing.

00:39.660 --> 00:41.920
We see here it has
a negative slope.

00:41.920 --> 00:45.620
Every time we move forward
3 in the x direction,

00:45.620 --> 00:49.180
we're going to move down 7
in the vertical direction.

00:49.180 --> 00:51.730
So neither of these
are increasing

00:51.730 --> 00:54.080
so that's definitely not right.

00:54.080 --> 00:55.400
f and g are both increasing.

00:55.400 --> 00:57.640
Well, that's
definitely not right.

00:57.640 --> 01:00.550
So we know that both f
and g are decreasing.

01:00.550 --> 01:03.390
So this first choice says
they're both decreasing, and g

01:03.390 --> 01:06.400
is decreasing faster than f.

01:06.400 --> 01:09.160
So let's see what
the slope on g is.

01:09.160 --> 01:14.380
So the slope on g is every time
we move 1 in the x direction,

01:14.380 --> 01:16.510
positive 1 in the
x direction, we

01:16.510 --> 01:21.460
move down 2 in the y direction.

01:21.460 --> 01:25.990
So for g of x, if we were
to write our change in y

01:25.990 --> 01:29.750
over our change in x-- which
is our slope-- our change in y

01:29.750 --> 01:33.030
over change in x, when we
move one in the x direction,

01:33.030 --> 01:35.060
positive 1 in the
x direction, we

01:35.060 --> 01:38.120
move down 2 in the y direction.

01:38.120 --> 01:42.960
So our change in y over
change in x is negative 2.

01:42.960 --> 01:46.420
So g has a slope of negative 2.

01:46.420 --> 01:49.300
f has a slope of negative 7/3.

01:49.300 --> 01:56.120
Negative 7/3 is the same
thing as negative 2 and 1/3.

01:56.120 --> 01:58.870
So f's slope is more negative.

01:58.870 --> 02:01.070
So it is decreasing faster.

02:01.070 --> 02:04.520
So g is not decreasing faster
than f. f is decreasing faster

02:04.520 --> 02:05.020
than g.

02:05.020 --> 02:06.750
So this is not right.

02:06.750 --> 02:09.440
And then we have this choice--
f and g are both decreasing,

02:09.440 --> 02:12.010
and f is decreasing
faster than g.

02:12.010 --> 02:13.960
This is right, right over here.

02:13.960 --> 02:17.870
We have this last choice-- g is
increasing but f is decreasing.

02:17.870 --> 02:21.670
We know that's not true.
g is actually decreasing.
